<newsitem itemid="94204" id="root" date="1996-10-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>FRANCE: Colas doubles H1 net loss.</title>
<headline>Colas doubles H1 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six month to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable loss			324  vs   loss    161</p>
<p>    Net loss					 331  vs   loss    161</p>
<p>    Turnover				     8,134  vs	   8,142</p>
<p>NOTE - Roadbuilding company Colas gave its results in a statement. It said in the light of available information, sales for the 1996 year should be around 19.5 billion francs and net profit should around the same level as 1995. The company made 1995 net profit of 404 million francs. Colas is 59 percent owned by construction group Bouygues.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 PNT</p>
